  "description": "Inside Wants Out is the debut EP by American singer-songwriter John Mayer. Released by Mayer Music in 1999, the album was later re-released by Columbia Records on August 2, 2002, with the omission of \"Neon 12:47 AM\". Basic tracks were to be recorded at Full Moon Studio in Athens, Georgia. The songs \"Back to You\", \"No Such Thing\", \"My Stupid Mouth\", and \"Neon\" were later re-recorded for Mayer's 2001 full-length debut album Room for Squares.",
